From b8e2dbed50f8171a4bee3cb9ee1b84c4af9a2bea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cristian Ciocaltea <cristian.ciocaltea@collabora.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 21:52:33 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] drm/tests: hdmi_state_helper: Add HDMI 2.1 FRL mode
 validation coverage

Add tests to verify the Fixed Rate Link validation path introduced in
hdmi_clock_valid(), using the new test EDID that advertises HDMI 2.1 FRL
capability with 48 Gbps and max TMDS character rate of 600 MHz:

- drm_test_check_frl_rate_rgb_12bpc: check that for a 4K@60Hz RGB mode,
  when TMDS rate exceeds 600 MHz at higher bpc, the FRL path allows the
  mode at the highest supported bpc

- drm_test_check_frl_no_rate_valid_func: check that the mode is allowed
  at the highest supported bpc even without a .frl_rate_valid()
  callback, since that hook only narrows down the rates the source and
  the sink already agree upon

- drm_test_check_frl_reject_rate: check that when .frl_rate_valid()
  callback rejects all FRL rates, higher bpc modes fall back to 8bpc
  just as if FRL was not available

Signed-off-by: Cristian Ciocaltea <cristian.ciocaltea@collabora.com>
Link: https://gitlab.collabora.com/hardware-enablement/rockchip-3588/linux/-/commit/c1c6b535125c401967bb5bdf3b7dff516cb2f47b
